# Does identifying one wondrous item teach the KIND? Oracle for inc-dd5m.
#
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/wonder-idtype.keys 1
#
# Same shape as amulet-idtype.keys (read its header for why the In-the-Air line
# is the measurement). A Mandolin of Musical Defense is an AI_WONDER effect with no
# flavour. Take one unidentified, identify the pack, take a second, read both
# names. The ring is the control, as in the amulet script.
#
# [s] stows, ESC leaves the manager (ENTER does nothing once the cursor has
# moved to an empty belt slot).
#
# The SECOND item of each kind joins its matching stack in the pack (inc-j12i0
# automatic pickup), so no manager opens and nothing is left in the air. The
# measurement for the -2 dumps is the "AutoStowing: <name>." message line, not
# the In-the-Air line, and no [s] is sent for them.
#
# The WONDER count is an index into ItemGlyphs (src/Tables.cpp:320), from
# zero: wonder 39, ring 26.

@include chargen.keys

@dump:arrival

w
y
@choose "Acquire Unknown Item"
RIGHT*39
@until "Mandolin of Musical Defense" DOWN
ENTER
@dump:wonder-1-in-air
s
ESC

w
@choose "Acquire Unknown Item"
RIGHT*26
@until "Fire Resistance" DOWN
ENTER
@dump:ring-1-in-air
s
ESC

w
@choose "Identify Whole Pack"

w
@choose "Acquire Unknown Item"
RIGHT*39
@until "Mandolin of Musical Defense" DOWN
ENTER
@dump:wonder-2-in-air

w
@choose "Acquire Unknown Item"
RIGHT*26
@until "Fire Resistance" DOWN
ENTER
@dump:ring-2-in-air

@quit
